CAUSAL INTERPRETATION

LU-0 showed
that the historical global recruitment pool
creates an exact nonlocal dependency
in the V0.1 U-cell transition law.

LU-0B showed
that the dependency is active
on ordinary fresh Task-1 trajectories.

LU-0C then tested
a literal local recurrent replacement
against simple deletion.

In LU-0C:

NO_POOL passed the full preservation envelope;

LOCAL_POOL_R12 did not;

and LOCAL_POOL_R12 added no value over deletion.

LU-0D now repeats the NO_POOL result
on five independently derived worlds.

The confirmation passes every frozen criterion.

Therefore the evidence supports:

THE GLOBAL C/S RECRUITMENT-POOL CONTRIBUTION
IS NOT REQUIRED
TO PRESERVE THE VALIDATED V0.1 FUNCTIONAL ENVELOPE
UNDER THE TESTED DEVELOPMENTAL WORKLOAD.

This is now a replicated simplification result.

It does not prove
that no future task will ever benefit
from a broader recruitment signal.

It does establish
that the current hand-designed substrate
does not need this organism-wide dependency
to retain its validated Task-1 behavior.

