PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

We made the simpler organism
prove itself again.

Five new worlds.

No cherry-picking.

No changed thresholds.

No local substitute.

We simply removed
the organism-wide recruitment signal.

The simpler organism passed
every test we froze in advance.

It handled the starting workload.

It handled the workplace moving.

It handled demand reversal.

It handled damage.

It stayed correct.

It stayed within the work budget.

And in all five new worlds,
its final relocation-window completion
was actually higher
than the old global-pool version.

So the result from LU-0C was not a fluke.

We now have two independent five-world sets
showing that this global signal
can be removed.

That matters because the next learned cell
no longer needs to imitate
a behavior that secretly depends
on organism-wide information.

We have removed one real obstacle
to a genuinely local learned updater.

